Multimodal stacked ensembles were trained using development-cohort out-of-fold predicted probabilities after
participant-level aggregation and complete-case modality intersection. The neural-network meta-learner was
then evaluated on the corresponding held-out complete-case ensemble inputs. As described in the Methods, all
ensemble configurations were evaluated on the same internal held-out cohort of 90 participants with complete
data for all five analysed task types.
Table 3 summarises the held-out performance of BiLSTM and Conv1D-BiLSTM ensembles across four task
set configurations. Among all ensemble models, the Conv1D-BiLSTM Main Symptoms configuration,
combining Rest Tremor, GaitWalk, and PinchToSize, achieved the highest observed ranking performance,
with ROC AUC 0.9131 (95% CI 0.8439–0.9695) and PR-AUC 0.9354 (95% CI 0.8901–0.9822). The
Conv1D-BiLSTM Easy configuration, combining Rest Tremor, Postural Tremor, and Balance, achieved the
strongest binary classification performance at the exported evaluation rule, with Macro F1 score 0.8534,
accuracy 85.56%, sensitivity 73.33%, and specificity 97.78%. This configuration also had the lowest Brier
