sensitivity of classification metrics to class distribution, decision rules, and cohort composition. In PADS, the
majority-class accuracy baseline was 77.75%, compared with observed accuracies of 81.52% for Rest Tremor
and 77.47% for Postural Tremor. Because class prevalence differed across datasets and probabilities were not
recalibrated, Brier scores were interpreted within each dataset rather than compared directly across datasets.
