Thai data-protection regulations.
Code Availability
The full study-specific preprocessing, modelling, evaluation code, trained model weights, and derived
prediction files are not publicly available because they include project-specific data-ingestion, preprocessing,
and platform-integration components linked to governed CheckPD data. The manuscript and Multimedia
Appendix provide model architecture, preprocessing steps, hyperparameter ranges, validation procedures, and
evaluation metrics to support independent reimplementation. Non-sensitive implementation details or
pseudocode may be made available by the corresponding author on reasonable request, subject to institutional
approval.
Patient and Public Involvement
Patients and members of the public were not formally involved in the design, analysis, interpretation, or
writing of this retrospective modelling study. The broader CheckPD programme was implemented with
support from public health partners and participating communities, and participants contributed data through
programme activities. Future prospective validation should include structured patient and public involvement.
